WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.340
Ay, what's up my well-read ballas?
It’s 2015, Thug Notes is back,

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:20.260
and this week we gettin lonesome
with "The Raven" by Edgar Allan Poe.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:28.820
It’s a balls-cold December night in the hood,
where our narrator doin what all real gangstas do

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:33.320
when they tryna get their mind off a lost hunny-love –
Crack open a book. Holla!

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.320
Playa bout to pass out when he hear
a ruckus at the door and then he starts wiggin.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:42.180
He check it – nothin. Then homeboy hear an even
louder tappin and open his window,

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:47.000
when a raven flies his black ass in the crib
and posts up like he owns the damn place.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.160
Since he ain’t got nobody else to
talk to, the narrator say,

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:53.820
"Bird, what’s yo name?”
All da Raven gotta say is “Nevermore.”

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:58.480
Oh sh*t, this fool talks? Talk or not, the
narrator don’t really give no fu**s.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.940
There been other feathery bird bruthas up in his digs befo, and all just ended up leavin.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.820
When da Raven hear that, he just say, "Nevermore."

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.360
The hell?
Then our boy start thinkin,

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:13.280
“Maybe God tryna help me forget Lenore and
get dem thoughts of her sweet lovin outta my dome.”

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:16.380
“Nevermore.”
This muthafu**a. Then the narrator like,

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:20.640
“Okay. Real talk. Am I gonna
get to chill wit my girl in heaven after I die?"

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:26.300
Don't say– "Nevermore."
MUTHA FU**A! Get da hell outta here. Shoo!

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:30.060
But dat bird jus stonewallin him.
So da narrator throws in the towel

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.400
and accepts errything is so damn
jacked up dat he ain’t neva gonna be happy no mo.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.480
Damn.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:43.040
Dealin wit the death of a back-when biddy 
is sho as hell one depressing topic.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.580
On the real, tho, dat’s just what what Poe was goin for.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:50.000
In “The Philosophy of Composition,” Poe pretty much say the entire reason he wrote this poem

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.460
was to depress the sh*t outta people.
Thanks, Poe. It worked.

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.340
He even break it down for us. 
So how can a brutha make somebody sad as hell?

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:03.780
Step 1: Talk bout death. But that ain’t enough a playa gotta make sho dat erryone can relate to dat pain.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:06.000
And what’s da saddest thing a brotha can lose?

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.200
You got it, son. Some of dat ooooweeeee.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:15.320
So BAM! Poe mix it all togetha and tell us his recipe for
da most melancholy juice you can ever sip on –

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.140
the death of a beautiful woman.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:19.120
Peep deez references playa play –

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.680
that raven can be referencin a couple of different mythological traditions.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:28.620
In Norse Myth, Odin got two ravens rollin in his posse
named Huginn and Muginn – Thought and Memory.

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:33.600
These little thuggies flew around and gave Odin the DL on what was goin down in da hood.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:38.420
In "The Raven," the narrator’s bird hookin him up with some info too, just not the good kind.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:41.240
Our boy havin to do his best to forget about Lenore,

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:46.640
but all dat punk-ass raven do is fill his head up with
thoughts and memories of that hunny. Damn.

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:51.500
Now for my Greek homies, ravens
were associated with prophecy and the god Apollo.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.180
Maybe that’s why da raven is described as “ominous” –

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:58.900
cuz he's related to omens and hintin
that some gnarly sh*t bout to go down.

00:02:58.910 --> 00:03:04.120
Speakin of da future, Poe bitch-slappin us with the raven sayin “nevemore” ova and ova.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:08.740
Thang is, our narrator start off sayin the exact opposite: “Forevermore.”

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:14.920
But by the end, he and that funky bird droppin da same beat, sayin dat his soul gonna be lifted “nevemore.”

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:19.240
To this thug, that's emphasizin the
connection between the raven and da narrator.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:24.860
they jus gonna sit they sad, lonely asses at home
sayin da same thing over and over again.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:29.360
Don’t think it’s a coincidence, too,
that "nevermore" rhyme with "Lenore," yo.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:33.640
See y’all next week, my well-read ballas.
Sparky Sweets out. Peace.

